cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use TripLibre in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "TripLibre: An Open-Source, Privacy-First Travel Diary for Mobility Research"
abstract: >-
  TripLibre is an open-source, local-first iOS application designed for personal
  mobility tracking and travel behavior research. It records
  location data in the background, reconstructs daily travel activities
  into visits, trips, transportation modes, and trip chains. It allows
  users to review and correct inferred travel records. The application
  supports exporting structured mobility datasets in CSV, JSON, GeoJSON,
  and SQLite formats, with a Python loader for further analysis.

  By combining automated GPS-based travel detection with user-controlled
  data management, TripLibre aims to lower the technical and financial barriers
  to collecting travel behavior data. Its broader vision is to provide
  researchers, educational institutions, and resource-constrained
  communities with an accessible and adaptable alternative to proprietary
  travel survey technologies, while preserving individual control over
  sensitive location information.
